    "precisionJustification": "PLANNED COVERAGE, NOT OBSERVED DATA. This layer is the planned Galactic Plane Survey (GPS, 9 maps), derived by Assets from STScI pre-generated healsparse exposure-time maps in spacetelescope/roman_notebooks (pinned commit cb3ec341a1ff, APT program 1430, whose status may be Draft). The union of every pixel with a finite value above zero in 9 input map(s) (nside_sparse 4096, NESTED) is stored as a MOC at order 12; decoded area 808.18 deg2 in 126580 cells. The STScI-published figure is about 691 deg2; the map-derived area (808.18 deg2) is larger and the cause of the difference is not confirmed. The roll angle of the pre-generated maps may not match on-orbit exposures. No Roman survey data exist yet, so there are no files to look up; this is a planned extent, not a per-band valid-pixel mask or an observed footprint.",
